WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.559
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:09.129
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:16.389
Unit eight: Business News Basics. Today you will describe trends with rose by, fell to and increased from.

4
00:00:16.689 --> 00:00:19.504
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.734
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:25.863
Earnings report.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.614
Earnings report means a company's official statement of the money it made.

8
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.820
The earnings report surprised investors.

9
00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:37.336
Your turn. Say: Earnings report.

10
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.515
Earnings report.

11
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.692
Quarterly results.

12
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:48.633
Quarterly results means financial results published every three months.

13
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.853
Quarterly results showed strong growth.

14
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.300
Your turn. Say: Quarterly results.

15
00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.471
Quarterly results.

16
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:01.229
Shareholder.

17
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:05.017
Shareholder means a person who owns part of a company.

18
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:07.860
Every shareholder received a dividend.

19
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:11.625
Your turn. Say: Shareholder.

20
00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:15.456
Shareholder.

21
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:17.102
Merger.

22
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:21.312
Merger means the joining of two companies into one.

23
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:24.032
The merger created a larger bank.

24
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.909
Your turn. Say: Merger.

25
00:01:29.767 --> 00:01:30.733
Merger.

26
00:01:31.483 --> 00:01:32.798
Profit margin.

27
00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:37.908
Profit margin means the percentage of sales left after costs are paid.

28
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:41.132
A higher profit margin means better earnings.

29
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.520
Your turn. Say: Profit margin.

30
00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.472
Profit margin.

31
00:01:49.217 --> 00:01:50.044
Revenue.

32
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.791
Revenue means the total money a company receives from sales.

33
00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:57.766
Revenue grew as more customers arrived.

34
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.817
Your turn. Say: Revenue.

35
00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:04.505
Revenue.

36
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.448
CEO statement.

37
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.634
CEO statement means an official message from the head of a company.

38
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.679
The CEO statement promised new investment.

39
00:02:14.283 --> 00:02:17.981
Your turn. Say: CEO statement.

40
00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:22.078
CEO statement.

41
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:24.189
Market reaction.

42
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:29.145
Market reaction means how investors and prices respond to news.

43
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.738
The market reaction was calm.

44
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:35.014
Your turn. Say: Market reaction.

45
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:39.390
Market reaction.

46
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:43.886
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:50.885
Visal, this report says 'Revenue rose by eight percent to two billion dollars.' Why two different prepositions?

48
00:02:51.983 --> 00:03:00.801
'By' shows the size of the change and 'to' shows the new level. 'Profit fell from ten to eight million' gives the old and new figures.

49
00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:03.591
What other verbs can I use?

50
00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:14.673
Rose, increased, grew, fell, dropped and declined. Business headlines also say 'Shares slump' or 'Profits jump' to attract attention.

51
00:03:15.783 --> 00:03:17.191
And the market reaction?

52
00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:25.591
Reporters add it after the numbers: 'Shareholders welcomed the merger, and the share price climbed.'

53
00:03:26.733 --> 00:03:28.408
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:33.246
Grammar focus: Trend language: rose by and fell to.

55
00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.791
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:35.483 --> 00:03:37.494
Revenue rose by eight percent.

57
00:03:38.383 --> 00:03:40.534
Profit fell to eight million dollars.

58
00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.274
Sales increased from two million to three million.

59
00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:54.280
Use 'by' for the size of a change, 'to' for the new level, and 'from' for the old level: rose by 8%, fell to $8 million, increased from 2 to 3.

60
00:03:55.017 --> 00:03:58.505
Be careful! Don't say: Sales rose to five percent.

61
00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:03.058
Say: Sales rose by five percent.

62
00:04:03.358 --> 00:04:05.393
Use 'by' for the size of the change.

63
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.852
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:11.051
Company Results.

65
00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:14.732
Business news reports a company's results in clear numbers.

66
00:04:15.733 --> 00:04:20.856
In its quarterly results, the company said revenue rose by eight percent to two billion dollars.

67
00:04:21.867 --> 00:04:27.187
The profit margin fell slightly, but the CEO statement promised lower costs next year.

68
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.474
A planned merger also pleased every shareholder, and the market reaction was positive.

69
00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:38.080
Readers should compare the numbers before they judge the earnings report.

70
00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:43.563
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.544
Revenue rose blank eight percent.

72
00:04:46.844 --> 00:04:49.522
A, by. B, of. C, at.

73
00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:54.857
The answer is A: by.

74
00:04:56.017 --> 00:04:58.272
The joining of two companies is a blank.

75
00:04:58.572 --> 00:05:01.737
A, merger. B, margin. C, verdict.

76
00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.102
The answer is A: merger.

77
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.946
A person who owns part of a company is a blank.

78
00:05:11.246 --> 00:05:15.550
A, reporter. B, shareholder. C, consumer.

79
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.982
The answer is B: shareholder.

80
00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:25.476
Profit fell blank eight million dollars.

81
00:05:25.776 --> 00:05:28.652
A, to. B, by of. C, in.

82
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.327
The answer is A: to.

83
00:05:35.483 --> 00:05:38.795
According to the reading, the market reaction to the merger was…

84
00:05:39.095 --> 00:05:42.516
A, positive. B, angry. C, unknown.

85
00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.380
The answer is A: positive.

86
00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:52.300
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.972
What kind of business news would affect your decision to buy a company's stock?

88
00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:07.887
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:08.187 --> 00:06:26.565
News about a company's earnings would affect my decision most. If revenue and profit margin rise steadily, I would feel more confident. A merger or a strong CEO statement could also matter, although I would check the facts first. I would never decide from one headline alone.

90
00:06:26.865 --> 00:06:28.690
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:29.583 --> 00:06:35.266
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and trend language: rose by and fell to.

92
00:06:35.566 --> 00:06:41.156
Today's value is financial literacy. Understand money well enough to make wise decisions.

93
00:06:41.456 --> 00:06:43.725
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:44.025 --> 00:06:46.445
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

